DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20240316T130000
DTSTAMP:20240301T045136Z
URL:https://anandaportland.org/events/aging-consciously-workshop-part-1/
SUMMARY:Aging Consciously Workshop\, Part 1
DESCRIPTION:Read Nayaswami Hanuman's inspiring letter about this class HERE
 .\n\nThis course is intended to bring light and awareness of how to naviga
 te challenges and find joy and peace in the later years of life.  For man
 y\, growing older can be a time of renewed spiritual purpose\, deepening m
 editation and refining our relationship with God.\n\nOn a physical and mat
 erial level\, the aging process may also be a time of coping with our own 
 and loved ones' health challenges\, loss of loved ones and ultimately beco
 ming more dependent upon family or caregivers to assist us with personal c
 are as the body declines. These difficulties can also be meaningful pathwa
 ys for personal and spiritual growth at this stage of life.\n\n\n\n&nbsp\;
 \n\n In this class you will learn:\n\n 	How to become pro-active about ag
 ing  \n 	How to transcend our fears\, and resistance to Elderhood  \n 
 	How to prepare for inevitable loss that life brings\, including: loss of 
 a spouse\, our  friends\, our health\, and our sense of security.  \n\n
 Unique aspects of this class: \n\n 	We will be working together\, doing s
 mall group activities  \n 	There will be ample time to share your story 
 and personal challenges you  are facing  \n 	Together we will create a 
 sacred space where we can take those initial steps into  Elderhood in a c
 onscious way. \n\n*****************************************\n\nWith decade
 s of experience and insights\, Nayaswami Hanuman and Jan Jerome will share
  wisdom and tools to approach the later years with a sense of positive exp
 ectation and peace\, while planning and following practical strategies to 
 prepare ourselves and our loved ones for the times ahead.  The key to bei
 ng at peace with the changes that aging inevitably brings is preparing wis
 ely for these years\, while living everyday to the fullest\, trusting in G
 od.\n\nThis workshop is planned to be two parts\, to enable participants t
 o work on end-of-life planning and to have a follow up with Hanuman and Ja
 n in one month. \n\nThe second workshop is scheduled for April 13 @ 11 am
 . Payment for this class includes the second class. \n\nSliding scale fee
  - please register below.\n\nLed by Nayaswami Hanuman BSN and Jan Jerome M
 SW.\n\nAbout Nayaswami Hanuman:\n\n\n\nI have been a nurse since 1976 and 
 an Ananda minister for over 30 years. My primary interest has been in the 
 physical\, mental\, and spiritual wellbeing of those who I have had the pr
 ivilege of serving. For 25  years I was a hospice nurse and co founded An
 anda House\, an elder care home for like minded people searching for meani
 ng in their lives through Kriya Yoga. \n\nMuch of what I do is to educate
  and facilitate care management of people in need through partnering  wit
 h the greater health and social services community. \n\nI am a member of 
 the Ananda healthcare team in the United States. By partnering with other 
 nurses and health ministers throughout our broader community we hope to ed
 ucate and inspire others in the best possible way to live a happy and heal
 thy life in our elder years.\n\nAbout Jan Jerome: \n\n\n\nHello\, my name
  is Jan Jerome and I have been an Ananda member for over 30 years.  I was
  blessed to receive Kriya in Seattle in 1989.  For the past 30 years\, we
  have lived in the Denver\, CO area and my husband and I moved to Oregon i
 n 2023.  We are thrilled to be close to the Ananda Portland Temple and ot
 her devotees. \n\nI am a licensed clinical social worker and have spent m
 y career providing counseling\, care management\, palliative care and well
 ness education services in medical/mental health settings serving older ad
 ults and persons living with chronic and life limiting conditions.  \n\n&
 nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://anandaportland.org/wp-content/uploads/20
 24/01/Joe-and-Bill.jpg
CATEGORIES:Classes,workshop
LOCATION:Ananda Portland Temple\, 4855 SW Watson Ave\, Beaverton\, OR\, 970
 05\, United States
