 spine with a brief meditation following the asanas.\nWe are made of energy
 ! Join us to feel energized for the weekend.\nAnanda Yoga® is gentle and 
 our instructors encourage and support appropriate modifications so all bod
 ies can participate safely. Come early to class and speak with the instruc
 tor about your needs. \n$15.00 per class\n$10.00 per class:  Senior disc
 ount for 60 years old +\n\nDrop-ins welcome. Preregister and prepayment op
 tional.\n\n***************************************************************
 ***\n\nPurchase a 10 class package and save!\n(packages must be purchased 
 on site)\n\n$15 per drop-in / 10 class package $135\, get 1 class free/$13
 .50 per class) good for 1 year.\n\n$10 Senior rate (10 class package $90\,
  get 1 class free/ $9.00 per class) good for 1 year.\n\n\n\n&nbsp\;\n\nMel
 issa Heart has been teaching Ananda Yoga since 2012 as a certified Ananda 
 Yoga instructor. She’s been with Ananda Portland since 2007 and has serv
 ed in many capacities at the temple. Currently she serves as a member of t
 he ministry team\, manager of the temple and coordinator for Education for
  Life Outreach Programs.\n\n**********************************************
 *****************************\n\nReview of Ananda Yoga – Beaverton OR.\n
 From: Rick Cady - Tualatin\, OR. \n\n"As a current student of Ayurveda\, I
  had been looking to complement my studies with a Yoga tradition that woul
 d support the ideals espoused by the ancients related to the Yoga sciences
 . Given that the Western model of Yoga tends toward only a focus on the ph
 ysical aspects of the practice\, I was happy to find a more traditional pr
 actice of Hatha Yoga through the Ananda Temple here in Beaverton\, OR. Tea
 cher Melissa Heart brings this practice to life with her unique and effect
 ive teaching style with an emphasis on being conscious and still as we mov
 e into poses\, hold the pose\, and come out of the pose. This practice emp
 hasizes utilizing the poses to relax the body and be aware of our state of
  mind to ultimately prepare for meditation. Melissa is a gem that I am gra
 teful to have met\, as you can feel her love for the practice and desire t
 o share it with others. On a physical level\, I had been diagnosed many ye
 ars ago with a Lumbar spine defect that had given me significant pain and 
 limitations for several decades\, and this practice has made me virtually 
 pain free in about 3 months. A true miracle. I am forever grateful and wil
 l be a lifetime supporter of Melissa and Ananda Yoga."
