 ton\, OR\, 97005\, United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Ananda Portlan
 d Temple:geo:0,0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4002926@anandaportland.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20251115T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20251115T153000
DTSTAMP:20251111T015324Z
URL:https://anandaportland.org/events/the-wisdom-of-our-dreams-2025-11-15/
SUMMARY:The Wisdom of Our Dreams
DESCRIPTION:Our dreams speak a universal language that comes to us in the s
 ervice of health and wholeness.  It is believed that they originate from 
 the Self\, the divine within that not only supports the purpose of our exi
 stence\, but provides respite and guidance in our lives.  \n\nParamhansa
  Yogananda defines dreaming as “A subconscious state of mind when the pr
 ana is withdrawn from the senses and combine with the imagination\, which 
 is the visualizing ability of the conscious mind.”\n\nHe also said:  
 “Introspection is a mirror in which to see recesses of your mind that ot
 herwise would remain hidden from you.”\n\nIn this 2-morning workshop\, w
 e will discuss:\n\n- the history and spiritual tradition of dreams\n\n- wh
 y and how we dream\, and its different levels\, as explained by Yogananda\
 n\n- their purpose and function in our lives\n\n- how to remember\, record
  and incubate our dreams\n\n- using our dreams to deepen and guide our spi
 ritual journeys \n\n- ways to interpret our dreams and sacred symbols \n
 \n- how to extend a dream symbol through creative expression and active im
 agination \n\nThis workshop is in two parts held on November 8 and 15\n\n
 On the second morning\, you will have the opportunity to process a dream y
 ou have through the association method\, and if desired\, through a group 
 process.\n\nBring a significant\, recurring\, or recent dream and we’ll 
 process it together on the second morning.  And if you don’t have a dre
 am or even dream at all\, then this workshop will certainly inspire dreams
  to come to you for introspection and guidance.  \n\n&nbsp\;\n\nShubatan
 i Geri Grubbs\, Ph.D. is a practicing Jungian psychotherapist in Gaston\, 
 Oregon\, a devotee of Paramhansa Yogananda\, teacher and author of “Bere
 avement Dreaming and the Individuating Soul\,” published in 2004.  \n\
 n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://anandaportland.org/wp-content/uploads/20
 24/09/johannes-plenio-DKix6Un55mw-unsplash-scaled.jpg
CATEGORIES:Classes,workshop
LOCATION:Ananda Portland Temple\, 4855 SW Watson Ave\, Beaverton\, OR\, 970
 05\, United States
