URL:https://anandaportland.org/events/drop-in-ananda-yoga-with-melissa-202
 6-02-25/
SUMMARY:Drop-in Yoga for Beginners with Melissa
DESCRIPTION:No need to pre-register—just drop in and join us! This beginn
 er-friendly yoga class is designed for anyone curious about yoga or lookin
 g to build a solid foundation.\nWhat to Expect\n\n 	Gentle Guidance: We'll
  guide you through the basic poses of Ananda Yoga step by step.\n 	Accessi
 ble Practice: Perfect for all ages\, fitness levels\, and body types.\n 	
 Stress-Free Environment: A welcoming space to explore movement and breath
 .\n 	Flexible Schedule: Come when it works for you\; classes are open to 
 drop-ins.\n\nBenefits\n\n 	Improve flexibility and balance\n 	Reduce stres
 s and tension\n 	Build strength gradually\n 	Learn breathing techniques to
  calm the mind\n\nDetails\n\n 	Duration: 90 minutes (centering\, warm-ups
 \, asanas\, savasana &amp\; 10 min. meditation)\n 	What to Bring: Comfort
 able clothing\, a yoga mat (or borrow one at the Temple)\, and water.\n 	C
 ost per class : $15 regular/ Senior $10 (65+) you can get a session pack 
 discount too!\n\n\n Whether it’s your very first yoga class or you’re
  returning after a break\, this session is the perfect way to ease into pr
 actice.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n$15.00 per class\n$10.00 per class:  Sen
 ior discount for 60 years old +\n\nDrop-ins welcome. Preregister and prepa
 yment optional.\n\n*******************************************************
 ***********\n\nPurchase a 10 class package and save!\n(packages must be pu
 rchased on site)\n\n$15 per drop-in / 10 class package $135\, get 1 class 
 free/$13.50 per class) good for 1 year.\n\n$10 Senior rate (10 class packa
 ge $90\, get 1 class free/ $9.00 per class) good for 1 year.\n\n**********
 ********************************************************\n\n**************
 ****************************************************\nReview of Ananda Yog
 a – Beaverton OR.\nFrom: Rick Cady – Tualatin\, OR.\n\n“As a current
  student of Ayurveda\, I had been looking to complement my studies with a 
 Yoga tradition that would support the ideals espoused by the ancients rela
 ted to the Yoga sciences. Given that the Western model of Yoga tends towar
 d only a focus on the physical aspects of the practice\, I was happy to fi
 nd a more traditional practice of Hatha Yoga through the Ananda Temple her
 e in Beaverton\, OR. Teacher Melissa Heart brings this practice to life wi
 th her unique and effective teaching style with an emphasis on being consc
 ious and still as we move into poses\, hold the pose\, and come out of the
  pose. This practice emphasizes utilizing the poses to relax the body and 
 be aware of our state of mind to ultimately prepare for meditation. Meliss
 a is a gem that I am grateful to have met\, as you can feel her love for t
 he practice and desire to share it with others. On a physical level\, I ha
 d been diagnosed many years ago with a Lumbar spine defect that had given 
 me significant pain and limitations for several decades\, and this practic
 e has made me virtually pain free in about 3 months. A true miracle. I am 
 forever grateful and will be a lifetime supporter of Melissa and Ananda Yo
 ga.”
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://anandaportland.org/wp-content/uploads/20
 19/06/Satyana_Yoga-scaled.jpg
