URL:https://anandaportland.org/events/pg-wodehouse-readers-theater/
SUMMARY:PG Wodehouse Reader's Theater
DESCRIPTION:Sir Pelham Grenville Wodehouse  (15 October 1881 – 14 Februa
 ry 1975) was an English writer and one of the most widely read humorists o
 f the 20th century. His creations include the feather-brained Bertie Woost
 er and his sagacious valet\, Jeeves\; the immaculate and loquacious Psm
 ith\; Lord Emsworth and the Blandings Castle set\; the Oldest Member\
 , with stories about golf\; and Mr. Mulliner\, with tall tales on subject
 s ranging from bibulous bishops to megalomaniac movie moguls.\n\nSwami Kri
 yananda\, founder of Ananda\, shared PG Wodehouse stories and enjoyed the 
 good natured humor. Sharing laughter is good for the heart and soul!\n\nDe
 tails of the play and the readers will come soon.\n\nJoin us for our Indep
 endence Day BBQ potluck at 4 pm and stay for PG Wodehouse at 6 pm.  We ho
 pe to see you there!\n\n*Please pay whatever you want to give on a sliding
  scale.\n\n&nbsp\;\n\n&nbsp\;
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://anandaportland.org/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/02/PG-Wodehouse.jpg
